Package: kpqc
Type: Package
Title: Korean Post-Quantum Cryptography Algorithms
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("O.", "Suolfou", email = "osuolfou@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("SAMSUNG SDS", role = c("ctb", "cph")),
    person("Team HAETAE", role = c("ctb", "cph")),
    person("NTRU+ TEAM", role = c("ctb", "cph")),
    person("Team SMAUG-T", role = c("ctb", "cph")),
    person("Thomas", "Pornin", role = c("ctb", "cph"))
  )
Description: Synchronous interfaces to the AIMer and HAETAE signature
    schemes and the NTRU+ and SMAUG-T key encapsulation mechanisms (KEMs)
    selected by the Korean Post-Quantum Cryptography competition. Native
    reference implementations are compiled into the package and use
    operating-system entropy for key generation, signing, and encapsulation.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
URL: https://github.com/KpqC/kpqc-r
BugReports: https://github.com/KpqC/kpqc-r/issues
Depends: R (>= 3.6.0)
Encoding: UTF-8
SystemRequirements: C11
NeedsCompilation: yes
